  "result": "I added `truncateMiddle(text, max)` to `src/cli/truncate.ts` and committed it as `4543430`. The new tests pass and `npm run fast` passes.\n\n- **Behaviour:** Text that already fits is returned unchanged. Longer text keeps its start and end around a single `…`, so the result is never longer than `max`. When the characters kept can't split evenly, the start gets the extra one.\n- **Edge cases:** `max` of 0 or less returns an empty string, and `max` of 1 returns just `…`. It counts by code point, so emoji aren't split in half.\n- **Tests:** `test/cli/truncate.test.ts` covers fitting text, truncation, tiny limits and emoji.\n- **Shard weight:** I added the new test file to `scripts/lib/shard-weights.mjs` with a placeholder weight of 0.1, not a measured one.\n\nI didn't touch the task tracker.",
